  22: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  23:     """Recolor each foreground object according to how many enclosed background regions it contains.
  24: 
  25:     Input structure
  26:     - A background canvas with one foreground color forming several 4-connected objects.
  27:     - Each object is a filled rectangular blob with one to four enclosed background holes.
  28: 
  29:     Rule
  30:     - Preserve the background.
  31:     - Count the 4-connected enclosed background components inside each object's bounding box.
  32:     - Recolor the whole object by the learned hole palette: one hole -> blue, two -> red, three -> green, four -> orange.
  33: 
  34:     Key insight
  35:     - The internal holes are the only varying symbol; object size and absolute position do not determine the output color.
  36:     """
  37:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
